  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass m rests on a horizontal table with a co-efficient of static friction $\\mu .$ What minimum force must be applied on the block to drag it on the table?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "OXcIA",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu}{\\sqrt{1+\\mu^{2}}} \\mathrm{mg}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4LvNk",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu-1}{\\mu+1} \\mathrm{mg}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bVTrI",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu}{\\sqrt{1-\\mu^{2}}} \\mathrm{mg}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mUWcL",
      "text": "$\\mu \\mathrm{mg}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint:\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/E-Q3dXzUCPuAJnJDKUZD7UVE7YWcYpaYWWmKj_E9P-w.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n$F \\sin \\theta+N=m g \\quad N=m g-F \\sin \\theta$\r\n$F \\cos \\theta=\\mu(m g-F \\sin \\theta) \\quad F=\\frac{\\mu m g}{\\cos \\theta+\\mu \\sin \\theta}$,\r\nfor $F_{\\min }, \\frac{d}{d \\theta}[\\cos \\theta+\\mu \\sin \\theta]=0$\r\n$\\therefore \\tan \\theta=\\mu$\r\n$\\therefore F_{\\min }=\\frac{\\mu \\mathrm{mg}}{\\sqrt{1+\\mu^{2}}}$",
    "image": null
  },
